# Automotive

- Protocols never parse in an ISR. ISR copies a frame to a queue.
- UDS/DTC are shared services. BLE/UART/MQTT are transports, not a second diagnostic DB.
- Vehicle physics and product policy do not live in CAN drivers.
- Integrity failures (CRC, alive, timeout, range, plausibility) go to Fault Manager + DTC.
- Mark simulated IDs as prototype. Do not invent OEM databases.

ISO-TP and UDS already exist — harden with loss/timeout tests before rewriting.
Do not start BLE or cloud work until OSAL + POSIX HAL + CAN path are reviewed.
